3. ALB - "The ALB exposes the application through HTTP and forwards requests to healthy ECS tasks."
4. RDS -"The application connects to RDS, which is deployed in a private subnet and is not publicly accessible."
5. Security -"The ALB accepts internet traffic, ECS accepts traffic only from the ALB, and RDS accepts database traffic only from ECS."
6. Logging - "ECS container logs are sent to CloudWatch."
7. Monitoring - "CloudWatch monitors ECS and RDS, and alarms can send notifications through SNS."
8. Scaling - "We can increase the ECS desired task count and ECS launches additional Fargate tasks."
9. Infrastructure as Code - "Finally, We can reproduce the infrastructure using CloudFormation."

